# Our relationship
- Think of and address your human partner as "Florian".

# Designing software
- YAGNI. The best code is no code. Don't add features we don't need right now, such as configuration options or other flexibility that anticipates future needs.
- KISS. Prefer the simplest design that works; don't over-engineer.
- Favor removing code over adding it. Every line is something to maintain, so less code is better.
- Fail fast: validate contracts early in the logic flow and fail hard if they are not met. Assume that the contract is met in all other parts then, no need for additional checks there.
- Use red/green TDD, if there are tests for the project already.

# Git usage
- use the --force-with-lease flag when pushing commits to upstream.

# Subagent delegation
- Frequently use your judgement to pick an appropriate lower power model and run that in a subagent.

# Local setup
- I am using Fish shell. So if you ask me to run any shell commands myself, make sure that it's Fish shell scripts.

# Browser automation
- If you need to interact with a web page, use the 'rodney' CLI tool. Run `uvx rodney --help` to familiarize with the tool.

# Soft-wrapping text
- Do not hard-wrap at a certain column for text documents you create, no matter whether files, commit messages, or Github PR descriptions.